# Deployment artifact boundary.
#
# Product photography for the imported catalogue is ~640 MB across 7,700 files and belongs in object
# storage (ADR 0006), not in a deployment. The bytes are uploaded to the catalog bucket and
# `/catalog/<key>-<width>.<ext>` resolves to them through `src/app/catalog/[...path]/route.ts`.
#
# A handful of committed placeholder assets stay in the build because they are part of the repository
# and are served by `public/` before the route is reached.
# Every catalog raster (product photography, category photographs and brand marks) is delivered from
# object storage by `/catalog/[...path]`; only the small SVGs stay in the build so a placeholder still
# resolves without the bucket.
public/catalog/*.jpg
public/catalog/*.webp

# Local-only state that is never part of a deployment. Environment files hold credentials for this
# machine only; the deployment's values come from the project's environment variables.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev-pg/
.tmp-*/
.playwright-cli/
.codegraph/
.pi/
.next/
coverage/

# The owner's Android app is a separate build artefact: it is a Capacitor shell around the deployed
# panel, it is not served by this deployment, and it carries a 30 MB Gradle tree and an APK.
android-app/

# Documentation and the verification suites are not needed to serve the application.
docs/
tests/
scripts/
**/*.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
